<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ciudad Bolívar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ciudad Bolívar is the capital of Bolívar state in south-eastern Venezuela, on the south bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orinoco">Orinoco</a> at its narrowest point. Founded in 1764 as Angostura, it became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a>'s base in the war of independence: the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-angostura">Congress of Angostura</a> met there in 1819, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/correo-del-orinoco">Correo del Orinoco</a> was printed there. It was renamed in his honour in 1846.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ciudad-bolivar.jpg" alt="Ciudad Bolívar" width="320" height="206" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Venecon at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ciudad_Bol%C3%ADvar_historical_zone.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
